From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] Non-blocking and partial deferred-reply drains, serial-tied
 coherent invalidation, and cached memory properties

DeferredReplies::reserve() first reads any replies already waiting in the
device socket buffer (FIONREAD) and, when still above budget, drains only the
oldest prefix needed to halve the backlog rather than waiting on the newest
command just flushed. Coherent buffer GPU writes recorded on command buffers
are tied to the submission serial that executes them, so
cabooseInvalidateCoherentMappings invalidates only writes whose submission has
completed on the feed. vkGetPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties and
vkGetPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties2(KHR) (including
VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryBudgetPropertiesEXT) return from the ResourceTracker
cache after the first query.

